//# #3326: an `Array[X]` is not a generic struct applied to `X`.
//
// `Cell[Int]` resolves to an applied `CtNamed`, which `check_assignable`
// tolerated as a possibly-rigid head, and a builtin `Array` had no nominal
// name for `nominal_head_conflict` to compare. So this compiled clean and
// `x.value` read the array's packed representation (4294967554 for `[1]`).
// The plain `struct P { v: Int }` control was already rejected, and so was
// `Option[Int]` in the same slot.

struct Cell[T] {
  value: T
}

fn main() -> Unit allows Console {
  let x: Cell[Int] = [1]
  println(__to_string(x.value))
}
